  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1956-p30.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let the side length be \\(s.\\) From \\[ \\frac{s\\sqrt3}{2}=\\sqrt6, \\] we get \\(s=2\\sqrt2.\\) Hence the area is \\[ \\frac12s\\sqrt6 =\\frac12(2\\sqrt2)(\\sqrt6)=2\\sqrt3. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "For side length \\(s,\\) an equilateral triangle has altitude \\(\\frac{s\\sqrt3}{2}\\)",
        "Once \\(s\\) is known, use area \\(\\frac{sh}{2}\\)"
      ],
